# Microeconometrics Project – Credit Scoring Model

This project was developed as part of a Master’s degree coursework in Applied Economics at the University of Lille.

The objective of this project is to analyze and predict credit card subscription behavior using microeconometric and statistical methods.

The analysis focuses on a logistic regression model applied to credit scoring and consumer behavior prediction.

## Main Topics
- Binary logistic regression
- Credit scoring analysis
- Probability estimation
- Statistical interpretation
- Predictive modeling

## Tools Used
- R
- RMarkdown
- Econometric and statistical methods
- Data visualization

## Files Included
- R/RMarkdown code
- Final report (PDF)
- Dataset and predictions

This project reflects practical skills in microeconometrics, statistical modeling and quantitative data analysis.
